    {
      "value": "<p>The innermost catalogued moon of the giant, an ice body with a brine ocean under about eleven kilometres of shell and vent chemistry running in it. The surface is fractured and refrozen in overlapping lobes and gets a hard dose of radiation from the primary. Nothing lives on top; a great deal appears to live underneath.</p>",
